1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,234
Claude apps: you think ten Notion edits cost you ten trips to another tab, but actually, in supported apps, you never leave the chat.

2
00:00:08,534 --> 00:00:09,818
You watch Claude make them.

3
00:00:10,318 --> 00:00:11,342
Here's what changed.

4
00:00:11,642 --> 00:00:14,560
Before, Claude showed a small window: a live preview.

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:17,707
For the full editor, you opened Notion in another tab.

6
00:00:18,007 --> 00:00:20,144
Ten tasks: back and forth, ten times.

7
00:00:20,644 --> 00:00:25,069
Now, where supported, the whole Notion opens beside the chat, signed in as you.

8
00:00:25,369 --> 00:00:29,869
You ask once; Claude edits all ten tasks, and you see each change as it happens.

9
00:00:30,169 --> 00:00:31,383
You approve its actions.

10
00:00:31,883 --> 00:00:32,316
How?

11
00:00:32,616 --> 00:00:38,149
It's built on MCP Apps, an open extension: the tool brings its own screen into Claude.

12
00:00:38,649 --> 00:00:44,793
Asana, Canva, Notion and more, to start; rolling out on web and desktop, all plans, in the new Claude.

13
00:00:45,293 --> 00:00:52,857
So, what we learned: ten tasks used to mean ten trips to another tab; now, in supported apps, Claude edits them beside your chat.

14
00:00:53,357 --> 00:00:54,059
Want more?

15
00:00:54,359 --> 00:00:56,890
Subscribe, and comment what we should explain next.
